  "root_cause": {
    "text": "In the bonding network driver, `bond_header_parse()` relied on `skb->dev` to identify the bonding device context, but since `skb->dev` points to the hierarchy top in stacked bonding configurations, recursive calls failed to traverse to the leaf device, causing an infinite loop.",
    "evidence": "The patch adds a `const struct net_device *dev` parameter to `bond_header_parse()` and changes `netdev_priv(skb->dev)` to `netdev_priv(dev)`, while updating the recursive call to `slave_ops->parse` to explicitly pass `slave->dev` instead of relying on `skb->dev`.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
